  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Droitwich Excavation revealed the ruins of a Roman villa and an associated settlement as well as two winged corridor-type houses of the second century. The site received an earthwork in the third century. The site was occupied until the fifth century.</p>",
